class DefinitionType {
  definition {
    The strategy used to define a concept, per ISO 704:2022 §5.3.

    ISO 704 distinguishes four definition strategies:
      - intensional: genus + differentiae (the standard form)
      - extensional: enumerate instances or species
      - partitive:   describe composition (parts of the whole)
      - translated:  a definition translated from another language

    Glossarist carries the type as a wire field on DetailedDefinition
    so that tools can filter, validate, and render based on definition
    strategy.

    Default is intensional when omitted (backward-compatible with
    existing data).
  }
  values {
    intensional
    extensional
    partitive
    translated
  }
}
